<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/11th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty · Peace</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chanyuan Treaty</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1005">1005</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Chanyuan Treaty was a peace agreement concluded in 1005 between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty</a> and the Khitan <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao dynasty</a>. The Song agreed to pay annual tribute in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silk">silk</a> in return for peace along the northern frontier. It formalised a tributary relationship that brought long-lasting peace but left the northern territories in Liao hands.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chanyuan-treaty.jpg" alt="Chanyuan Treaty" width="280" height="307" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 玖巧仔 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Liao_and_Song_Dynasties.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
<section class="enc-quotes"><h2 class="enc-section-title">Across the Institute</h2><ul><li><blockquote>In 1004 the Empress Dowager Chengtian and Emperor Shengzong led an army deep into Song territory to <b>Chanyuan</b>, near the Yellow River, forcing the treaty that brought more than a century of peace.</blockquote><a href="/empire/liao-dynasty">Liao dynasty · Military</a></li><li><blockquote>…heartland after the fragmentation of the Five Dynasties and Ten Kingdoms period, though it never recovered the Sixteen Prefectures around modern Beijing held by the Khitan Liao dynasty, and under the <b>Chanyuan Treaty</b> of 1005 it agreed to costly annual payments of silk and silver to the Liao.</blockquote><a href="/empire/song-dynasty">Song Dynasty · Foundation</a></li></ul></section>
